{"name":"Pretty Posie","hex":"#bcbde4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pretty","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pleasant to the sight or other senses; attractive, especially of women or children. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Of objects or things: nice-looking, appealing."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Somewhat, fairly, quite; sometimes also (by meiosis) very.","Prettily, in a pretty manner."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pretty"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nosegay","blocks":[{"text":"A nosegay, posy, or tussie-mussie is a small flower bouquet. They have existed in some form since at least medieval times, when they were carried or worn around the head or bodice. Doilies are traditionally used to bind the stems in these arrangements. Alternatively, \"posy holders\", available in a variety of shapes and materials, enable the wearing of these arrangements \"at the waist, in the hair, or secured with a brooch\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/The_nosegay_LCCN2002710681.jpg/330px-The_nosegay_LCCN2002710681.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nosegay","wikidata":"Q14125324"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg/500px-Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg/1280px-Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg/500px-Holder%2C_bouquet_%28AM_67821-8%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bouquet holder","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHolder%2C_bouquet_(AM_67821-8).jpg"}],"sounds":{"pretty":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b2/En-us-pretty.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b2/En-us-pretty.ogg/En-us-pretty.ogg.mp3"}]}}}